{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books","id":1464816,"title":"starting V5 and wondering about the value of previous edition books...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-21T19:53:07-07:00","id":1464816,"title":"starting V5 and wondering about the value of previous edition books...","content":"so! sorry if this feels particularly 'noobish' but my only previous experience with VtM was getting the tzimisce book back when it first came out to get some inspiration for the 'chill' game i was running (and the only other white wolf books i had, back in the last century, was the 'werewolf: the old west' and 'specters' book for 'wraith' which i had for similar reasons.)<br /> that being said, i recently grabbed most of the V5 books (still need 'cults of the blood gods' and a few of the pod books) and i've been looking through what's available on drivethrurpg and, frankly, it's a bit overwhelming and i'm wondering what books from previous editions folks think can bring a great deal of value to a V5 game.<br /> (and i'm dreadfully sorry if this has been covered, already.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T20:11:41-07:00","id":1464818,"title":"","content":"A lot of them are fantastic and very useful to the setting still, especialy the V20 ones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T20:46:25-07:00","id":1464822,"title":"","content":"Beckett's Jyhad Diary is the predictable but solid answer here. The last V20 book, it's largely a metaplot/setting oriented book (Beckett is a famous NPC that's a historian and vampire-oriented anthropologist, so he's a frequent POV character for in-game fiction as he studies the world of vampires). It's also meant to help bridge the old setting and the setting as V5 stands.<br /> <br /> There's no reason BJD can't work in reverse of helping move from pre-V5 to V5. It's full of juicy bits that could be used to guide a V5 fan new to the game to look into old books that might cover topics they're interested in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T00:12:36-07:00","id":1464830,"title":"","content":"I also like the Revised Era Guide to the Sabbat and Guide to the Camarilla. They are much more detailed than their V5 counterparts (which are mainly fluff).<br /> <br /> V20, in general, has loads of useful info. The rules mostly transfer across (I convert Virtues so that Self-Control becomes Composure and Courage becomes Resolve; Appearance is just a Merit; use a vampire's recorded siring date and history to estimate Blood Potency, etc). Some things need a bit of creativity but with some familiarity you can eyeball it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T00:39:33-07:00","id":1464835,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Lore of the Clans</b></i> is outdated but still fantastic.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Anarchs Unbound</b></i> is a must-buy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T01:26:18-07:00","id":1464837,"title":"","content":"Once you go back you'll never... go back (to the present) <br /> <br /> Midnight seige. Hunters hunted II. Any of the Thaumaturgy books. The clanbooks. V1 or V20 core book. Werewolf corebook (any edition's good), Mage corebook (I don't know enough about the edition wars of mage, but M20's a mess with laughable editing and people hate revised for getting rid of the otherwords) <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464835#post1464835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Lore of the Clans</b></i> is outdated but still fantastic.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T01:54:11-07:00","id":1464838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464837#post1464837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a really well written book.<br /> <br /> As a note, I strongly suggest NOT getting <b>Hunters Hunted II</b> because that book basically does its best to roll back any progress the Hunters have made in the YEAR OF THE HUNTER books. It's very well written but it basically is, &quot;And then the hunters screwed up and the vampires won&quot; over and over again. The NSA guy dies a senile old man that no one believes, the SAD is reincorporated into the FBI and put on mundane serial killers, the Inquisition is now losing its faith because its legalized torture again, and so on.<br /> <br /> I love all OPP books but this one as a personal preference rubbed me the wrong way. It's still very well written but I have issues with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-22-2021, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T02:47:04-07:00","id":1464840,"title":"","content":"Hunters Hunted 2 &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; SI <br /> <br /> The SI is very nebulous and ill defined (and politically and logistically implausible but you're welcome to make the most of it because it just isn't well defined) HH2 gives you hunting organizations with character and depth. Hunters are flawed. Diverse, divisive, superstitious, magical or scientific. It puts a lot of light into &quot;Why don't vampires just do X&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:09:59-07:00","id":1464841,"title":"","content":"Revised sabbat is waaaaaaaaaaaayyyy better than v5 sabbat as is anarchs unbound. Caramilla revised is also useful but less so as the gap in quality is less severe than the other 2.<br /> <br /> V20 books are universally amazing, I'd also recommend midnight siege if you want a solid grasp of how vampiric warfare works","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:13:50-07:00","id":1464842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464841#post1464841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 books are universally amazing,</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Lore of the Bloodlines and most of Dark Ages V20 would like a word with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:15:40-07:00","id":1464843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464842#post1464842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, Lore of the Bloodlines and most of Dark Ages V20 would like a word with you.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah okay I'll conceed lore of bloodlines is mediocre but what's wrong with da20 outside of the bland art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:17:50-07:00","id":1464845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464840#post1464840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters Hunted 2 &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; SI</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Just...no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The SI is very nebulous and ill defined (and politically and logistically implausible but you're welcome to make the most of it because it just isn't well defined) HH2 gives you hunting organizations with character and depth. Hunters are flawed. Diverse, divisive, superstitious, magical or scientific. It puts a lot of light into &quot;Why don't vampires just do X&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The Hunters of HH2 are pretty much one group after another of bumbling idiots. It's a great book but the presentation of the groups is a direct contrast to the flawed but hyper-competent versions in PROJECT TWILIGHT, THE INQUISITION, and THE HALLS OF THE ARCANUM.<br /> <br /> As for the SI, we got a taste in the Camarilla book but I'm waiting until our second antagonist book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:48:07-07:00","id":1464851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464845#post1464845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> Just...no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, different strokes for different folks.<br /> <br /> Like MyWifeisScary, I strongly prefer Hunters Hunted II to any of the Second Inquisition V5 material precisely for the reasons Phipps tends to not like a lot of V20; it\u2019s metaplot agnostic and so leaves the Storyteller free to tell their own stories with their own characters (player and non-player) instead of what some book has pre-built for you and insistent metaplot that makes the game feel more like a railroad than a world your player\u2019s characters are meant to meaningfully influence.<br /> <br /> The other important point about Hunters Hunted II is that it\u2019s NOT an adversaries book like the upcoming SI is said to be and that Phipps would prefer. That means it focuses on opening up the setting to stories from the PoVs of mortal hunters (who for dramatic reasons SHOULD be underdogs and not hyper-competent powers that be) in addition to using them as antagonists against PC-tier vampires.<br /> <br /> In other words, Hunters Hunted II treats hunters like people and not just plot devices\u2026 and yes, that means they have flaws and sometimes screw up even as they try to do the right thing because \u201cwelcome to humanity.\u201d<br /> <br /> Hunters Hunted II is just an all around better sourcebook for building countless stories of your own, not just replaying the one some dev wrote for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T04:30:07-07:00","id":1464856,"title":"","content":"Hey folks? If OP wants to read pages of us arguing about our views on the books and how they mesh with our personal tastes... there's a few pages of threads of us (and us as in the specific users in this thread already) doing that. Can we try to focus on what the OP is asking for help on, and not drag them into our could-be-the-liner-notes of one of the prop books stuff? Good foot forward for the new poster and all.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> So, another recommendation: The V20 Companion. It's short, it's like on mechanics, but it covers three topics that are really useful to vampires and can easily be incorporated into V5:<br /> <br /> 1) Titles. A detailed discussion of the official (or not so official) titles within each of the main Sects. It's not nearly as thorough as the dedicated books, but it's a great expansion to the core material and helps give flavor to the differences in politics in how the Sects operate (though the Sabbat stuff doesn't really work with V5 Sabbat with the major changes therein, but it's still how the Sect was before the Beckoning and Gehenna War). There is an optional system that gives characters a limited-use dice bonus to an appropriate instance of a Status roll based on the sway of their title.<br /> <br /> 2) Prestation. This is a fairly good write up of the main currency of the undead: favors. It talks about how favor-trading works in each Sect, and how owning up to your chits when they get cashed in is enforced. Again, there's some easy to transfer optional mechanics, but it's a good primer for an essential part of vampire politics.<br /> <br /> 3) Technology. While moved even further along in V5, this second of the book discusses how vampires adapt (or not) to the rapidly changing technological landscape of modern humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T05:11:34-07:00","id":1464860,"title":"","content":"One thing to be said in favor of &quot;Hunters Hunted II&quot; it's that, if you want to learn about the various &quot;hunter&quot; organizations that predate the SI, but don't want to read a lot of books, it's a neat package. They're all there glossed over, plus some realy obscure ones that touch on other WoD lines and don't have a book of their own.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's great if you want to be very well versed about each one of them, but as an &quot;encyclopedia&quot; of sorts I think it does its job very decently. It may help a V5 player to flesh out a more varied SI, before the SI book comes out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T12:34:34-07:00","id":1464896,"title":"","content":"I apologize.<br /> <br /> In fact, clearly all the controversy shows that V20 HH is a GOOD sourcebook for a V5 game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T13:14:33-07:00","id":1464902,"title":"","content":"General Points on the earlier books: -<br /> <br /> - The mechanics are not compatible with V5 without conversion - Stats are different, Disciplines have been consolidated and changed, feeding mechanics and clan weaknesses altered, etc.<br /> - The V5 game world has changed significantly with the near-collapse of the Sabbat, the Camarilla both gaining and shedding clans, and the Anarchs resurgent. And the Second Inquisition, of course<br /> <br /> Of the V20 books: -<br /> - Lore of the Clans and Lore of the Bloodlines are still largely relevant, apart from the Hecata<br /> - Beckett's Jyhad Diary is stuffed to the brim with interesting characters and metaplot, although you may need to do some supplementary Googling. If you have any doubts about how deep and detailed this game world is, this book will dispel them.<br /> - Anarchs Unbound is outdated but it shows the Anarchs on the cusp of their breakout into the big time and might be valuable.<br /> <br /> The older third edition books, Guide to the Camarilla / Sabbat / Anarchs detail the Sects as they were early in the millennium, which may be useful for recent-historical games and depth of background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:34:25-07:00","id":1464920,"title":"","content":"Beckett's Jyhad Diary is so devoted to story threads from years of older game editions that I'm hesitant to recommend it to someone just coming to the game. It's a love letter, but an inessential one in my view.<br /> <br /> Revised Edition's Guides to the Camarilla and Sabbat are pure gold. They even get into their respective subject factions' legal systems. They're a bonanza of world building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T17:41:12-07:00","id":1464943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464902#post1464902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The older third edition books, Guide to the Camarilla / Sabbat / Anarchs detail the Sects as they were early in the millennium, which may be useful for recent-historical games and depth of background.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to Sabbat and camarilla revised/3rd I'd personally recommend prioritising their characterization over the v5 books were possible simply because they're a lot more nuanced and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-22-2021, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T22:33:55-07:00","id":1464971,"title":"","content":"Honestly, none of the previous editions are really all that necessary for a V5 game as a Player. The default starting character you'll make was embraced within the past ten years, which is at best a decade after any lore that appears in the older editions. As a Storyteller, to be honest, the older books aren't needed either. This edition was written with the intention for you not to need anything from prior editions. It didn't build on the meta-plot from edition to edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T22:47:14-07:00","id":1464972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464943#post1464943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regards to Sabbat and camarilla revised/3rd I'd personally recommend prioritising their characterization over the v5 books were possible simply because they're a lot more nuanced and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely suggest going with V5 Camarilla. Infinitely more useful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T02:31:00-07:00","id":1464983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464972#post1464972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely suggest going with V5 Camarilla. Infinitely more useful.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mostly it just provides mechanics for the assamites and makes the sect dumber and nastier. Carmarilla are my favourite sect and It's quite well written I'll conceed but the mustache twirling v5 indulges in on behalf of the anarch centric setting is a dead weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T02:35:35-07:00","id":1464984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464983#post1464983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly it just provides mechanics for the assamites and makes the sect dumber and nastier. Carmarilla are my favourite sect and It's quite well written I'll conceed but the mustache twirling v5 indulges in on behalf of the anarch centric setting is a dead weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The evil Camarilla was already pretty well-established in Revised, though. It's not an invention of V5. Remember the Camarilla has an official position for murdering/torturing Thin Bloods, Caitiff, and Unclaimed vampires (Scourge).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T03:37:08-07:00","id":1464990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464984#post1464984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The evil Camarilla was already pretty well-established in Revised, though. It's not an invention of V5. Remember the Camarilla has an official position for murdering/torturing Thin Bloods, Caitiff, and Unclaimed vampires (Scourge).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes certainly, all the sects are evil when you think on it. The difference is revised they were pragmatic evil when in v5 they're stupid evil. Like the sabbat they all lack a lot of the nuances now.<br /> The second part is categorically false their was no formal policy of harming thin bloods or caitiff. It was genrally Princes discretion and frankly killing/capturing unknown vampires in a domain is probably a good idea when you consider the masquarade and the ongoing war.<br /> It isn't an issue of morality it's an issue of intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-23-2021, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T05:15:52-07:00","id":1465001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464837#post1464837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you go back you'll never... go back (to the present)<br /> <br /> Midnight seige. Hunters hunted II. Any of the Thaumaturgy books. The clanbooks. V1 or V20 core book. Werewolf corebook (any edition's good), Mage corebook (I don't know enough about the edition wars of mage, but M20's a mess with laughable editing and people hate revised for getting rid of the otherwords)</div> </div> </div> </div>The VtM Clanbooks are great, each takes a distinctly different approach in putting across a particular Clan. The 1st edition MtA Corebook is wonderful, overall I think it might be the best book in regard to the overall quality and mood of the illustrations. They wonderfully show the idea of Mages being special, powerful, and capable. Some particular VtM illustrations might be more noteworthy, but they are scattered across VtM books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-23-2021, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T06:57:43-07:00","id":1465006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zahana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1464971#post1464971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, none of the previous editions are really all that necessary for a V5 game as a Player. The default starting character you'll make was embraced within the past ten years, which is at best a decade after any lore that appears in the older editions. As a Storyteller, to be honest, the older books aren't needed either. This edition was written with the intention for you not to need anything from prior editions. It didn't build on the meta-plot from edition to edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about being necessary, but about adding value. Of course it isn't necessary, it isn't in any edition either.<br /> <br /> To say it didn't build on the metaplot is objectively wrong. It may not be how many players wanted, but it is a direct continuation of the metaplot.<br /> <br /> Many previous supplements can add value as they add ideas, interpretations and lore that the ST can wove into the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T09:31:16-07:00","id":1465016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1465006#post1465006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about being necessary, but about adding value. Of course it isn't necessary, it isn't in any edition either.<br /> <br /> To say it didn't build on the metaplot is objectively wrong. It may not be how many players wanted, but it is a direct continuation of the metaplot.<br /> <br /> Many previous supplements can add value as they add ideas, interpretations and lore that the ST can wove into the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its in my opinion, we're a lot of the flaws with the writing came from. The soft reset of the setting has produced a lot of issues, such as the lasombra defection being gibberish or the antitribu being an overt retcon anyway. They'd probably been better of either doing a hard reset or developing the setting less dramatically from revised. Of coarse a hard reset carries a lot of the developing issues over anyway....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-23-2021, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T10:53:41-07:00","id":1465019,"title":"","content":"The truly honest answer is that if you're going to do V5, you do not need any previous material, other than maybe some minuscule tidbits of fluff here-and-there. V5 is so far removed from the other editions, its not even funny. No Elders, 5 capped disciplines, Attributes have been changed to CofD style attributes, the god-awful Touchstone system, retcons/retrocons galore, horrible changes in some clans, metaplot is completely different, the internal logic of the franchise is different, etc.<br /> <br /> If you're going to primarily play V5, you just need V5 since its just a reboot of Classic World of Darkness to be geared to be more Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T13:08:23-07:00","id":1465031,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">A warning about edition warring. It's hard to identify sometimes but it is a relevancy.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T17:58:38-07:00","id":1465071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1465019#post1465019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truly honest answer is that if you're going to do V5, you do not need any previous material, other than maybe some minuscule tidbits of fluff here-and-there. V5 is so far removed from the other editions, its not even funny. No Elders, 5 capped disciplines, Attributes have been changed to CofD style attributes, the god-awful Touchstone system, retcons/retrocons galore, horrible changes in some clans, metaplot is completely different, the internal logic of the franchise is different, etc.<br /> <br /> If you're going to primarily play V5, you just need V5 since its just a reboot of Classic World of Darkness to be geared to be more Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that's generally been the way i'm looking at it but i'm looking at things like 'beckett's...,' 'ghouls and revenants,' and 'hunters hunted 2' to be able to sort of pad the world out a bit more (and the revised nofersatu and tzimisce clanbooks since the pcs will be interacting a lot with the former and the major antagonists will be the latter.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:00:48-07:00","id":1465072,"title":"","content":"(and i have ZERO interest in previous editions, as far as rules go, because v5 is the edition already decided on by my group, unanimously., and am mostly just interested in decent ideas/fluff/history that i can incorporate.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T00:03:17-07:00","id":1465100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1465072#post1465072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and i have ZERO interest in previous editions, as far as rules go, because v5 is the edition already decided on by my group, unanimously., and am mostly just interested in decent ideas/fluff/history that i can incorporate.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the books you list are all useful. I would add Revised Guide to the Sabbat, too, since the Sabbat has been gutted due to the metaplot. It gives you more options to see what they were like before they were put on a bus, and then you can pick and choose what to carry forward (especially if you have a Tzimisce in the game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T01:54:18-07:00","id":1465106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1465071#post1465071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> that's generally been the way i'm looking at it but i'm looking at things like 'beckett's...,' 'ghouls and revenants,' and 'hunters hunted 2' to be able to sort of pad the world out a bit more (and the revised nofersatu and tzimisce clanbooks since the pcs will be interacting a lot with the former and the major antagonists will be the latter.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to know and explore the setting better, then I definitely recommend <i>Counsel of the Primogen. </i>Through the lens of the office, the book does a great job of providing information and insights into how Camarilla politics and arrangments work, how Elders think and consider matters, and how the Kindred establish themselves in regard to influence and capabilities. It even has some additional Disciplines, and also discusses each of the Clans separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T06:59:03-07:00","id":1465132,"title":"","content":"oh, that one hadn't been on my radar, at all, so thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T07:56:56-07:00","id":1465138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1465072#post1465072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and i have ZERO interest in previous editions, as far as rules go, because v5 is the edition already decided on by my group, unanimously., and am mostly just interested in decent ideas/fluff/history that i can incorporate.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was most people's assumption here, at least was mine.<br /> <br /> Most old books will have something to offer, but generally speaking the suggestions already give you a good direction. V20 books will generally be more helpful for your time, with good broad, and still reasonably complete, treatments of various subjects. From there it is easier to position yourself and make an informed decision on where to go next.<br /> <br /> Given your interest in getting books that can give you more ideas and details to work with, you'll probably end up getting most books from every edition at some point, but each one will give you enough for your investment, so you don't need to rush yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T10:21:55-07:00","id":1465418,"title":"","content":"so! my shopping list, so far:<br /> 'clanbook nosferatu: revised.'<br /> 'clanbook tzimisce: revised.'<br /> 'clanbook baali.'<br /> 'midnight circus.'<br /> 'world of darkness: blood dimmed tides.'<br /> 'the book of nod.'<br /> 'revelations of the dark mother.'<br /> 'erciyes fragments.'<br /> 'nosferatu: the beast that haunts the blood' (yes, technically for 'requiem' but i think it has a lot of good stuff i can use.)<br /> beckett's jyhad diary.'<br /> 'v20 ghouls &amp; revenants.'<br /> 'v20 companion.'<br /> 'v20 children of the revolution.'<br /> 'v20 anarchs unbound.'<br /> 'v20 rites of blood.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T19:11:44-08:00","id":1470754,"title":"","content":"also! when it comes to the revised clanbooks, are any of them of any real value for v5, at this point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T19:42:52-08:00","id":1470758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464816-starting-v5-and-wondering-about-the-value-of-previous-edition-books?p=1470754#post1470754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also! when it comes to the revised clanbooks, are any of them of any real value for v5, at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the information on them is about clan history, how they organize and other similar fluff. Although not everyone pay heed to their description, yes, they're still a valid read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avata